<title>RUSSIA: LUKoil plans further rise in oil output in 1997.</title>
<headline>LUKoil plans further rise in oil output in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's biggest oil company OAO Neftyanaya Kompaniya LUKoil said on Monday it planned to raise oil production further to 59.7 million tonnes this year from a likely 58.3 million tonnes in 1996.</p>
<p>It said pretax profit, according to preliminary estimates, had risen to 3.7 trillion roubles in 1996 from 3.425 trillion in 1995.</p>
<p>It issued the following figures to Russian accounting standards.</p>
</text>
